# Import of the tokalign working tree -- the proof-of-concept alignment library
# that PRD 1.2 describes and that ADRs 0001-0004 are derived from. 194 MB on
# disk, ~90% of it a `.venv` and a mypy cache. Deny-by-default, as with the other
# three imports: nothing is tracked unless named below.
#
# The layout follows `.scratch/dl/`: this file sits one level *above* the
# imported repository, so `align-poc/` holds our own analysis `.md` files beside
# `tokalign/` rather than inside it. That is not only tidiness -- `!/*.md` below
# means "our writing", and with the policy one level down it also matched
# tokalign's own `TODO.md` and `TODO.human.md`, silently tracking another
# project's planning docs as though they were ours.
#
# The repo-root `.gitignore` still applies underneath these rules, and is what
# keeps `.venv`, `.mypy_cache/`, `.pytest_cache/`, `build/`, `*.egg-info/`,
# `__pycache__/` and `.DS_Store` out even inside re-included directories. Do not
# restate those here; a negation added below could re-admit them by accident.
#
# --- THIS FILE IS PHASED ------------------------------------------------------
# `.scratch/` is no longer deleted when this branch merges: it stays as the
# migration source for `hmm` and `align` 0.1.0 as well. So the tracked set is
# scoped to *the package currently being migrated*, and widens when that changes.
# The phases below are ordered by PRD 11 implementation order. Exactly one is
# active; switching means uncommenting the next block, not re-deriving it.
#
#   Phase 1  dataseq   DONE     -- the `Alphabet` encoder only; rules retained
#   Phase 2  hmm       ACTIVE   -- nothing here; `hmm` is seeded from hmm-lush
#   Phase 3  align     inert    -- the algorithms, the .pyx, the backend registry
#
# Keeping the inert rules written but commented is the point: the reasoning for
# what `align` will need was worked out while the tree was in front of us, and
# re-deriving it in three months' time would cost more than the comments do.
#
# Advancing to Phase 2 on 2026-09-01 added no files, and that is the finding
# rather than an oversight: nothing in tokalign is HMM-related, so Phase 2 was
# written empty by design and advancing into it is a pointer move.
#
# Phase 1's rules are *retained* rather than removed, and not merely out of
# tidiness. The tracked set can only widen. `.gitignore` is consulted only for
# files git does not already track, so re-commenting Phase 1 would change nothing
# about what is in the index; actually untracking those five files would take a
# `git rm --cached`, which is a deletion commit and re-opens the squash-merge
# hazard that retention stands down. See
# `docs/design/adr/0014-scratch-retention-and-per-package-scoping.md`.
#
# --- EIGHT RENAMES WERE NEEDED ON IMPORT --------------------------------------
# The most of any import so far; `hmm-lush` needed none. Three nested
# repositories and five agent-instruction files, all recorded in
# `.scratch/README.md` with their revisions, which were captured *before*
# disabling:
#   tokalign/{.,tokalign-dev,dev/plugins/workflow-claude}/.git -> .git-disabled
#   the same three directories' CLAUDE.md                      -> CLAUDE.md.orig
#   tokalign/AGENTS.md, tokalign/AGENTS.override.md            -> *.orig
#
# The `AGENTS.md` pair matters beyond the usual reason. That project uses the
# same agent-docs toolchain as pfsmgraph, so those two files are not merely
# another project's instructions -- they are the *generated artefacts* of one,
# and the `protect-agent-docs.py` hook matches on filename, so under their
# original names they would have been treated as this repository's own.
#
# `tokalign/dev/plugins/workflow-claude/` is a vendored clone of the same plugin
# this repository uses, and its directory is mode 555. Renaming a child needs
# write permission on the parent, so its two renames required `chmod u+w` first;
# the mode was restored to 555 afterwards. Anyone re-running this import needs to
# know that, because the failure is a bare "Permission denied" that looks like a
# sandbox restriction rather than a file mode.

# --- deny everything at this level -------------------------------------------
/*
!/.gitignore

# Our own writing about the import -- an ANALYSIS.md and anything joining it.
# Easy to forget and it fails silently: a file written here without this
# negation is simply invisible to `git status`, so the work looks committed and
# is not. It has now caught out two of the four imports.
!/*.md

!/tokalign/
/tokalign/*

# Narrative context and the declared build/runtime dependencies. `pyproject.toml`
# is tracked in every phase: it is the evidence for what `align` will need at
# build time (PRD 6.1 records `setuptools.build_meta` with `cython`/`numpy`,
# which ADR 0008 replaces with meson-python), and `docs/plan/DEFERRED.md` makes
# that a live question rather than a historical note.
!/tokalign/README.md
!/tokalign/pyproject.toml

!/tokalign/src/
!/tokalign/tests/
/tokalign/src/*
!/tokalign/src/tokalign/
/tokalign/tests/*

# =============================================================================
# Phase 1 -- dataseq  (DONE -- rules retained; see the header)
# =============================================================================
# Only the encoder. `Alphabet` is a bidirectional string <-> integer mapping over
# multi-character symbols, and [ADR 0010](../../docs/design/adr/0010-dataseq-composition-merging-three-implementations.md)
# names reconciling it with the merged encoder as *part of* this merge rather
# than a later question -- the two express the same thing. It is also the only
# one of the four implementations that already agrees with ADR 0011 on the points
# that matter: `encode` raises `KeyError` on an unseen symbol (strict by default),
# there is a real `gap_index`, and `decode` exists. What it needs is renumbering,
# not repair: `RESERVED_INDICES = 3` puts padding/BOS/EOS at 0-2, gap at 3 and
# user symbols at 4, where ADR 0011 inserts `UNK` and `MSK` and moves users to 6.
/tokalign/src/tokalign/*
!/tokalign/src/tokalign/__init__.py
!/tokalign/src/tokalign/_types.py

# Tracked only because `tests/conftest.py` imports it, and pytest loads that
# conftest for the whole `tests/` tree -- so without it `test_types.py` does not
# run. It is independently worth reading as the origin of ADR 0003's backend
# discovery, which is Phase 3's concern.
!/tokalign/src/tokalign/_backends.py

!/tokalign/tests/conftest.py
!/tokalign/tests/test_types.py

# =============================================================================
# Phase 2 -- hmm  (ACTIVE -- inert by design; nothing to add)
# =============================================================================
# `hmm` 0.1.0 is seeded from `.scratch/hmm-lush/`, not from here. This section
# exists so its emptiness is a recorded finding rather than an oversight: nothing
# in tokalign is HMM-related. It was made active on 2026-09-01 and added nothing;
# `.scratch/hmm-lush/` is where the `hmm` migration reads from, and its policy is
# already scoped to the whole live library, so it needs no widening either.

# =============================================================================
# Phase 3 -- align  (inert -- uncomment when align migration begins)
# =============================================================================
#
# ONE EXCEPTION, ADVANCED EARLY ON 2026-09-01. The reserved-block renumbering
# (`refactor/reserved-block-renumber`) had to audit every hard-coded index
# assumption in the alignment code, and the finding was a negative one: there is
# none. `_python.py` takes `gap_index: int` as a parameter and the caller feeds it
# `alphabet.gap_index`, so the algorithms are index-agnostic and the renumbering
# is confined to `_types.py` under Phase 1.
#
# A negative finding needs a signature to be checkable, which is the same reason
# `.scratch/py-rudimentary/.gitignore` tracks one file from `SegAlign-Draft`. So
# `_python.py` is tracked now and the rest of the phase stays inert.
#
# `_cython.pyx` deliberately stays untracked: `docs/plan/DEFERRED.md` keys the
# meson-python switch to "the first `.pyx` lands", and a `.pyx` under `.scratch/`
# belongs to no distribution and must not appear to fire it.
#
# The two `__init__.py` files are not tracked either, so this is evidence rather
# than an importable package. Both are 0 bytes; add them when Phase 3 advances.
#
# A SECOND FILE FOLLOWED, LATER THE SAME DAY. `test_needleman_wunsch.py` is tracked
# because the renumbering broke it and the fix had to be reviewable. Its helper read
# `alphabet.symbols[idx - 4]` and its 46 call sites wrote user symbols as codes from
# 4 -- a convention that collided head-on with ADR 0011 putting GAP at 4, so
# `_idx_to_sym(4)` returned the gap symbol instead of the first user symbol and 30 of
# 36 algorithm tests failed. The fix rebases the convention onto 0-based ordinals over
# `alphabet.symbols`, so these tests no longer encode where user codes begin and
# survive any future change to the block.
#
# Worth recording: the sources really are index-agnostic, but their *tests* were not,
# and no grep for `gap`/`GAP`/`== <int>` finds `symbols[idx - 4]`. Running the suite
# is what surfaced it. Baseline before the change was 62 passing; it is 62 again.
#
# The three rules below are what let git descend: `/tokalign/src/tokalign/*` in
# Phase 1 already excluded `algorithms/`, and git does not look inside an excluded
# directory, so a lone negation on the file would match nothing at all.

!/tokalign/src/tokalign/algorithms/
/tokalign/src/tokalign/algorithms/*
!/tokalign/src/tokalign/algorithms/needleman_wunsch/
/tokalign/src/tokalign/algorithms/needleman_wunsch/*
!/tokalign/src/tokalign/algorithms/needleman_wunsch/_python.py

!/tokalign/tests/algorithms/
/tokalign/tests/algorithms/*
!/tokalign/tests/algorithms/test_needleman_wunsch.py

# This is the bulk of the library and the reason the import was kept. Everything
# below is deliberate, not a leftover:
#
#   scoring.py            EMPTY (0 bytes). This entry previously described
#                         "substitution/affine-gap scoring built on ScoringMatrix";
#                         `ScoringMatrix` is in `_types.py`, tracked under Phase 1.
#                         Corrected 2026-09-01 by measurement.
#   algorithms/_registry.py
#                         five lines mapping one algorithm name to one module path.
#                         The backend dispatch ADR 0003 and ADR 0004 describe is in
#                         `_backends.py` (Phase 1, tracked), not here. Corrected
#                         2026-09-01.
#   algorithms/needleman_wunsch/_python.py
#                         the pure-Python phase-1 implementation. TRACKED -- see the
#                         exception above.
#   algorithms/needleman_wunsch/_cython.pyx
#                         the phase-2 kernel. ADR 0002 calls this "explicitly the
#                         reference template for future kernels and wavefront
#                         passes", so it is the single most load-bearing file
#                         here, and the first `.pyx` in this repo triggers the
#                         meson-python switch in DEFERRED.md
#
# Uncommenting the block below is idempotent: `algorithms/`, `needleman_wunsch/`
# and `_python.py` are already live above, and a repeated negation changes nothing.
# !/tokalign/src/tokalign/scoring.py       # 0 bytes -- see the inventory above
# !/tokalign/src/tokalign/algorithms/
# /tokalign/src/tokalign/algorithms/*
# !/tokalign/src/tokalign/algorithms/*.py
# !/tokalign/src/tokalign/algorithms/needleman_wunsch/
# /tokalign/src/tokalign/algorithms/needleman_wunsch/*
# !/tokalign/src/tokalign/algorithms/needleman_wunsch/*.py
# !/tokalign/src/tokalign/algorithms/needleman_wunsch/*.pyx
# !/tokalign/tests/algorithms/
# /tokalign/tests/algorithms/*
# !/tokalign/tests/algorithms/*.py
# !/tokalign/tests/test_scoring.py       # 0 bytes -- see the inventory above
# !/tokalign/setup.py      # the Cython build_ext invocation ADR 0008 replaces
# !/tokalign/benchmarks/   # 4 files; evidence for the phase-2 speedup claim

# --- deliberately not tracked in any phase, with reasons ---------------------
#
#   .venv/, .mypy_cache/     119 MB + 55 MB. Root rules exclude both.
#   build/, src/*.egg-info/  Compiled output and packaging metadata.
#   .git-disabled/ x3        5.6 MB, still readable with
#                            `git --git-dir=<path>/.git-disabled log`.
#   TODO.md, TODO.human.md   tokalign's own planning docs, 32 KB. Another
#                            project's plan, and the reason this policy sits one
#                            level up -- see the header.
#   tokalign-dev/            9.9 MB. A *separate* repository for that project's
#                            agent tooling, not part of the library.
#   dev/                     67 files, incl. a vendored clone of the same
#                            workflow-claude plugin this repo already installs.
#   docs/                    52 files. tokalign's own design notes. Superseded
#                            for our purposes by PRD 1.2 and ADRs 0001-0004,
#                            which were written *from* this library -- so where
#                            the two disagree, ours is the later word. Worth
#                            re-reading before the align migration, while the
#                            tree is still on disk.
#   Dockerfile.dev, .envrc, uv.lock
#                            Environment for a project we are not building.
#   CLAUDE.md.orig, AGENTS.md.orig, AGENTS.override.md.orig, .claude/
#                            Another project's agent instructions, generated
#                            artefacts and tool configuration. See the header.
